meta {
  name: Create Content
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/contents
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "body": "<p>Open a record to review its details.</p>",
    "content_category_id": "{{content_category_id}}",
    "cover_image_id": "{{file_id}}",
    "excerpt": "Read the administration guide.",
    "title": "Getting started"
  }
}

docs {
  ## Purpose

  Creates a content entry.

  ## Authentication

  Requires a valid access token with the `contents.create` permission.

  ## Behavior

  - Supply a title, excerpt, nonempty rich-text body, category ID and public cover image ID. Use a supported raster image uploaded with `context=contents`.
  - The body preserves the supported headings, emphasis, block quotes and lists. Links retain their text. Embedded content and other markup are removed.
  - The server generates the content UUID.

  ## Response

  - `201 Created` — Content created successfully.
  - `400 Bad Request` — Required content data is missing or invalid.
  - `401 Unauthorized` — Authentication is missing or invalid.
  - `403 Forbidden` — The authenticated user lacks the required permission.
  - `404 Not Found` — The selected category or public cover image is unavailable.
}
